  "slug": "assembly-read-1791",
  "summary": "Eight preprints benchmark upstream choices and redesign reconstruction steps for assembly, phasing, circular RNA, mtDNA and modification calling.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is controlling error at the reconstruction step instead of correcting it downstream. Two benchmarks test upstream choices directly: local assembly consensus strategies for long-read structural variant calling depend on read type and error profile, and polymerase choice affects HiFi assembly contiguity and completeness, with combinations improving results. Method-level designs follow the same logic. GRASER phases short reads on pangenome graph alignments using haplotype-unique edges to reduce reference bias. TERRACE 2.0 pairs outward and chimeric reads for circular RNA assembly. MitoArc adds NUMT-aware filtering and shifted-coordinate processing for mtDNA. NanoHIV-DR yields consensus and read-level resistance profiles, and an inosine model evaluation uses an ADAR-deficient control. Catch*ReSeq targets rare splice isoforms linked to single-cell transcriptomes. Newer here is the pairing of explicit validation controls with these designs.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-sonnet-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-25"
}
